	<tr>
		<td width="150" align="left" valign="top" class="row2"><span class="name"><a name="13184"></a><b>Reis</b></span><br /><span class="postdetails">Guest<br /><br /><br /><br /><br /></span><br /></td>
		<td class="row2" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=13184&amp;sid=8f91c21c5a7fce9c65085f4c95cba1e8#13184"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Tue Dec 04, 2001 3:08 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=13184&amp;sid=8f91c21c5a7fce9c65085f4c95cba1e8"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Courage may be part.. another curiosity.. another weakness, another boredom.. I suppose the list of causes is endless.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
In any case, what is important now is where I stand. Not so much with the light as with one foot on each side. I belive I stand the middle ground, because thier are things I admire about the darkness and the light. And if they are two sides of the same coin, then walking the middle path would be all the better. Right?
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Thier is no 'taint' in Tier'Dal blood. We are still the same as a race as we have allways been- creatures of a single aspect. The switch of aspects is irrelevent. I have Tunare's blood in my viens, too.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Thier is only life. Life that is chaotic, dangerous, filled with beauty, love, hate, and everything else. What people don't understand is that nothing is innately 'wrong'. That is what absolute viewpoints do to you. You ask how we are different- I don't think we really are. We're all made from the same elements. If you need some answer, well then here: in Neriak only Innoruuk is known. Everthing else is denied. If course you will find those who follow Rallos Zek, Solusk Ro, and some others. But only Innoruuk is known. To be different, to change, you have to admit first that it's possible, and that change, while it may not allways be for the better, is nessisary sometimes. I mean really know this. I'm sure that thier are many who say this is true, but when they worship Hate and only Hate, or War, or whatever, they only know this one thing and they deny themselves everything else. I have simply stopped worshiping one single thing. In unity you find the All. 
<br />
<i>You know your never sure
<br />

<br />
But your sure you could be right
<br />

<br />
If you held yourself up to the light</i><i></i></span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
