		<td class="row2" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=13188&amp;sid=8f91c21c5a7fce9c65085f4c95cba1e8#13188"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Fri Dec 07, 2001 3:03 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=13188&amp;sid=8f91c21c5a7fce9c65085f4c95cba1e8"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">My Lady Reis is the better of all of us Morelen. She is what all of us who stand to the side we call ‘Good’ wish to be, but can’t stomach. She accepts all ways of life as valid. Were she finds the courage to do so is beyond me. But I try to learn from her. As such my sword only swings at those who actively oppose the freedom and rights of others. Teir’Dal who do not force their ways on others have nothing to fear from me. It is the Gods job to know your heart and judge your souls not mine. I am simply that which defends those who chose to walk in the light, from those who would bar their path. But as I grow, I’ve learned that the sword is not the proper answer to simple words. Your ideas cannot harm those who have truly embraced the light, and any they might sway… Then they have failed the test that you represent. 
<br />
<i></i><br />_________________<br />Parnhamien Tor'Dainal
<br />
Paladin of Marr
<br />
Elder Concordat Angelis</span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
