		<td class="row2" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=13190&amp;sid=8f91c21c5a7fce9c65085f4c95cba1e8#13190"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Sat Dec 08, 2001 4:00 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=13190&amp;sid=8f91c21c5a7fce9c65085f4c95cba1e8"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Reis grins quietly as Rithnok speaks, then nods a little.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;Yes.. well it is still true that maybe ninty percent of people don't care for much beyond tomorrow's meals.. not that thier is anything inherently bad with that..&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Her attention then turns to Parnhamien, and she gives him the proudest smile as she listens to him speak, then finaly she looks twords Morelen.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;I had long since left Neriak by the time I had started thinking such things. But I do see your point.&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
She smiles.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;Now that you have plenty to think of, it might be best to find a spot you could think, away from the concern for your life that comes from liveing in Neraik. In Nektulos, I found such a place on the highest rocky peak. Sometimes the stars would shine through the fog, and you would see them as bright will-o-whisps hanging in the sky. I suppose that shows how determined the druids that have taken up residence in the woods are. But this particular hill has been very kind to my thoughts and the thoughts of friends i've had in the past..&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Reis trails the last sentance off, her gaze kind of floating downward. She then snaps her gaze forward suddenly and smiles.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;Thier is much more to many things that people think. And I don't see why we must be enemys. As I have said, I stand with one foot in the light and one in the dark. Many times fighting is counter productive, and I think this may be one of those cases.&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Reis smiles once more and offers an outstretched hand to Morelen. 
<br />
<i>You know your never sure
<br />

<br />
But your sure you could be right
<br />

<br />
If you held yourself up to the light</i><i></i></span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
			</tr>
